 post-ack recovery remain unfinished, with production acceptance flags false.
+
+
+Production standalone `service::run` (including `fsm execute`) and the
+embedded MCP `ExecutorLoop` now construct `Runner::new_native`, so fresh
+handler work uses the same retained preparation, writer-held claim and
+explicit Bound-entry sequence as native-selected public ticks; unavailable
+or unsupported native authority refuses work with `exec/mode`, without direct
+process/MCP startup or synthetic acknowledgement. Public low-level callers
+can still explicitly choose the legacy `Runner::new` primitive; production
+host constructors do not make that selection. This source routing change is
+provisional and does not establish production acceptance: exact-source native
+standalone/embedded tests, prior domain-semantic regressions, cold post-ack
+recovery, bounded shutdown and reconciliation remain required, and all
+production acceptance flags remain false.
